1
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:14,125
(Ryu Se-il)

2
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:22,042
(Ha Jung-hoon)

3
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:29,417
(Lee Jung-chan)

4
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:36,625
(Jung Si-wan)

5
00:00:44,917 --> 00:00:46,708
"Boy, with Caution"

6
00:00:50,792 --> 00:00:54,042
Whenever you see words like "ideal,"
think ethical perspective. Memorize that.

7
00:00:54,417 --> 00:00:59,750
When you put all of these together,
you get the "integrated perspective."

8
00:00:59,875 --> 00:01:02,833
Integrated perspective.

9
00:01:05,625 --> 00:01:09,750
Alright, how many perspectives
look at human society?

10
00:01:32,625 --> 00:01:34,545
You're the only one who
turned in a blank sheet.

11
00:01:36,708 --> 00:01:38,333
I didn't have anything to write.

12
00:01:39,750 --> 00:01:41,125
Then write "none."

13
00:01:41,417 --> 00:01:44,042
No dream college, no career goals.

14
00:01:44,167 --> 00:01:46,625
Just explain clearly
why you don't have any.

15
00:01:47,542 --> 00:01:49,022
Turn it in before the end of the day.

16
00:02:01,625 --> 00:02:06,917
"Boy, with Caution"
(Episode 2)

17
00:02:07,917 --> 00:02:12,000
Looks like it's my turn
to ask for your help.

18
00:02:12,125 --> 00:02:14,833
Mr. Jang always seems busy during lunch.

19
00:02:15,583 --> 00:02:16,750
Tell me about it.

20
00:02:16,875 --> 00:02:18,595
There's always something going on at lunch.

21
00:02:19,833 --> 00:02:21,375
About that phone...

22
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:23,208
Did Hyeon-jae really steal it?

23
00:02:24,292 --> 00:02:25,500
We don't know yet.

24
00:02:26,417 --> 00:02:29,083
Didn't they say they found
it in Hyeon-jae's backpack?

25
00:02:32,333 --> 00:02:35,042
Sometimes kids from
wealthy families act out.

26
00:02:35,167 --> 00:02:36,375
Just like this.

27
00:02:38,125 --> 00:02:39,750
I still need to talk to him.

28
00:02:39,875 --> 00:02:42,208
What's there to talk about?

29
00:02:44,083 --> 00:02:45,958
Just send him to the
disciplinary committee.

30
00:02:46,083 --> 00:02:47,875
The chairman will handle it anyway.

31
00:02:59,083 --> 00:03:00,250
Are you heading out?

32
00:03:00,375 --> 00:03:02,000
I have a meeting with Young-moon.

33
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:09,875
He's getting on my nerves more and more.

34
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:12,625
You know that type, right?

35
00:03:13,875 --> 00:03:16,250
The kind who never backs down
no matter what anyone says.

36
00:03:27,083 --> 00:03:28,917
He's the one who searched his own bag

37
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:30,708
and pulled my phone out of it.

38
00:03:30,833 --> 00:03:33,000
Why am I the one being called in?

39
00:03:33,417 --> 00:03:35,958
You just got here, Mr. Jang,
so you might not know.

40
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:38,167
Do you know why he's older than us?

41
00:03:38,292 --> 00:03:40,417
Word is it had to do with drugs.

42
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,542
He got expelled for dealing at school.

43
00:03:42,667 --> 00:03:43,500
And?

44
00:03:43,625 --> 00:03:45,059
Is that why you wanted to check
if he was carrying drugs?

45
00:03:45,083 --> 00:03:46,250
What?

46
00:03:47,708 --> 00:03:49,875
Because this kind of thing happens
every exam season.

47
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,333
Freshman year...

48
00:03:52,458 --> 00:03:53,792
Sophomore year, too...

49
00:03:56,583 --> 00:03:59,167
Every single perpetrator had drug issues.

50
00:04:04,167 --> 00:04:05,292
Mr. Jang.

51
00:04:05,417 --> 00:04:07,833
Doesn't it say right there
that I was the victim?

52
00:04:07,958 --> 00:04:10,000
Those bastards were the ones doing drugs.

53
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:11,875
What does that have to do with my phone?

54
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,792
They took the drugs,

55
00:04:14,917 --> 00:04:16,637
yet your grades were the ones that went up.

56
00:04:19,125 --> 00:04:23,000
What does that have to do with any of this?

57
00:04:28,833 --> 00:04:30,250
If Hyeon-jae admits he stole it,

58
00:04:30,375 --> 00:04:32,208
I'll send him to the
disciplinary committee.

59
00:04:33,583 --> 00:04:34,750
Mr. Jang.

60
00:04:35,167 --> 00:04:37,292
You know he's the chairman's son, right?

61
00:04:37,875 --> 00:04:42,667
Are you taking his side and
giving him special treatment?

62
00:04:45,542 --> 00:04:46,708
Yes.

63
00:04:47,250 --> 00:04:48,833
If you're done, head back to class.

64
00:04:49,292 --> 00:04:50,812
And send Hyeon-jae in on your way out.

65
00:04:56,625 --> 00:04:57,875
Want me to open that for you?

66
00:05:08,083 --> 00:05:09,792
Just pay him off.

67
00:05:09,917 --> 00:05:11,157
Give Choi Young-moon the money.

68
00:05:11,833 --> 00:05:13,833
I hear you're always
picking fights with him.

69
00:05:15,208 --> 00:05:17,208
Is that why you called me here?

70
00:05:18,292 --> 00:05:20,542
You keep causing trouble.

71
00:05:21,375 --> 00:05:23,000
Too many eyes are on you.

72
00:05:24,292 --> 00:05:27,542
If word gets around,
do you think the chairman won't find out?

73
00:05:28,792 --> 00:05:30,667
Then make sure it doesn't get out.

74
00:05:30,792 --> 00:05:33,375
All you have to do is play dumb
in front of my father.

75
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:39,167
I'm always on your side, of course.

76
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:44,208
But that new homeroom teacher of yours...

77
00:05:45,042 --> 00:05:46,292
He's just a sub.

78
00:05:46,417 --> 00:05:48,337
And he's only ever been
on short-term contracts.

79
00:05:49,958 --> 00:05:50,833
So?

80
00:05:50,958 --> 00:05:53,667
People with nothing to lose
are the hardest to deal with.

81
00:05:57,125 --> 00:05:59,625
He doesn't have to kiss up to anyone.

82
00:06:00,833 --> 00:06:02,583
You get what I'm saying, right?

83
00:06:03,292 --> 00:06:05,542
If this actually goes to
the disciplinary committee,

84
00:06:05,667 --> 00:06:08,750
my hands will be tied.

85
00:06:10,167 --> 00:06:11,708
When have you ever helped me?

86
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:16,000
I'm going to my meeting.

87
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:18,625
What meeting?

88
00:06:19,708 --> 00:06:21,417
Didn't you tell me to go pay him off?

89
00:06:22,958 --> 00:06:24,250
Right...

90
00:06:25,625 --> 00:06:27,792
You really go off the rails sometimes.

91
00:06:28,792 --> 00:06:32,292
How much is a phone
even worth? Why steal it?

92
00:06:32,417 --> 00:06:33,917
It's not like you need the money.

93
00:06:36,583 --> 00:06:37,875
Exactly.

94
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:57,208
Some things you can only say to a stranger.

95
00:06:57,917 --> 00:06:59,958
Have you ever felt like that?

96
00:07:20,875 --> 00:07:23,167
I have.

97
00:07:30,375 --> 00:07:32,583
When I wanted to run away.

98
00:07:35,167 --> 00:07:36,250
Run away?

99
00:07:54,417 --> 00:07:55,792
There you are.

100
00:08:04,375 --> 00:08:05,750
Mind if I sit here?

101
00:08:05,875 --> 00:08:07,208
I have a free period.

102
00:08:12,292 --> 00:08:15,583
Don't you get bored sitting here alone?

103
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:21,208
Why would school be boring?

104
00:08:32,125 --> 00:08:33,500
I don't think that.

105
00:08:37,042 --> 00:08:38,667
School isn't boring.

106
00:08:39,292 --> 00:08:41,500
You haven't turned in your
counseling sheet, have you?

107
00:08:43,333 --> 00:08:45,417
I haven't finished filling it out...

108
00:08:46,958 --> 00:08:48,292
Which part are you stuck on?

109
00:08:50,958 --> 00:08:52,292
The reason.

110
00:08:53,875 --> 00:08:55,875
The reason I have no goals.

111
00:08:57,458 --> 00:08:59,625
Is it too embarrassing
to let anyone see?

112
00:09:03,667 --> 00:09:05,833
I don't have one, but I'm
forced to make something up.

113
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:09,000
I stole that phone.

114
00:09:09,875 --> 00:09:11,458
Can't I just pay for it?

115
00:09:13,167 --> 00:09:14,458
Why?

116
00:09:16,208 --> 00:09:17,625
I'm asking why you stole it.

117
00:09:19,250 --> 00:09:21,042
Does that need a reason too?

118
00:09:21,167 --> 00:09:22,458
Yes.

119
00:09:24,667 --> 00:09:27,042
A phone isn't a pen cap
you just grab by accident.

120
00:09:45,667 --> 00:09:48,458
Figured you hadn't eaten lunch yet.

121
00:09:48,583 --> 00:09:54,250
Eat this, then hand in your sheet.

122
00:09:56,583 --> 00:09:57,833
Okay.

123
00:09:58,667 --> 00:10:00,250
If you don't want to say it out loud,

124
00:10:00,375 --> 00:10:03,083
write the reason you stole
the phone on that sheet.

125
00:10:04,667 --> 00:10:05,958
I'll get going.

126
00:10:07,417 --> 00:10:08,583
Mr. Jang.

127
00:10:12,208 --> 00:10:14,792
Are you always like this?

128
00:10:17,875 --> 00:10:20,042
Do you treat every student...

129
00:10:21,625 --> 00:10:23,292
with the same amount of care?

130
00:10:27,625 --> 00:10:29,083
Call it special treatment.

131
00:10:30,542 --> 00:10:32,292
Because I'm the chairman's son?

132
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:34,708
No.

133
00:10:35,583 --> 00:10:37,458
Because you look like you have nothing.

134
00:10:39,375 --> 00:10:41,095
Those are the only students I look out for.

135
00:10:42,250 --> 00:10:43,750
Students like you.

136
00:10:45,875 --> 00:10:47,125
See you around.

137
00:10:49,208 --> 00:10:50,848
Make sure you stop by the nurse's office.

138
00:11:21,917 --> 00:11:23,042
Hey!

139
00:11:35,167 --> 00:11:36,727
You didn't go to the hospital, did you?

140
00:11:39,125 --> 00:11:41,708
No training until you
bring in a doctor's note.

141
00:11:43,417 --> 00:11:44,000
Let me try one more time.

142
00:11:44,125 --> 00:11:45,875
What if you ruin your wrist?

143
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:47,375
I'll be careful.

144
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,333
Where do you get
this attitude? Huh?

145
00:11:52,417 --> 00:11:54,917
You're competing on someone else's dime.

146
00:11:55,042 --> 00:11:57,333
At least take it
seriously, you little brat!

147
00:12:00,125 --> 00:12:02,445
You think you got that
sponsorship because you're special?

148
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:04,417
I'm sorry.

149
00:12:18,708 --> 00:12:20,667
(Incoming Call: Grandma's Hospital)

150
00:12:27,625 --> 00:12:30,208
Hello, is this the family of Lee Jung-nam?

151
00:12:32,208 --> 00:12:34,125
I'm calling from the hospital.

152
00:12:34,250 --> 00:12:35,333
Speaking.

153
00:12:37,958 --> 00:12:39,292
How is my grandmother?

154
00:12:39,833 --> 00:12:43,167
Her condition hasn't been improving,

155
00:12:43,292 --> 00:12:45,833
so we'd like to discuss
transferring her to another facility.

156
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:51,083
(Medical Bill: Approx. 1,280,000 KRW)

157
00:12:54,417 --> 00:12:55,518
Looking for a fist to the face too?

158
00:12:55,542 --> 00:12:56,875
Spit it out.

159
00:12:58,167 --> 00:12:59,292
Lee Hyeon-jae.

160
00:13:00,667 --> 00:13:02,375
I'm not asking you to kill him.

161
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,167
Just bloody his face up a bit.

162
00:13:04,292 --> 00:13:06,667
That's all it takes.

163
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:10,083
Jang Gi-woo is blatantly
giving him special treatment.

164
00:13:10,208 --> 00:13:11,408
It's seriously pissing me off.

165
00:13:13,458 --> 00:13:14,833
How much are you offering?

166
00:13:14,958 --> 00:13:16,333
Jeong-ha.

167
00:13:16,458 --> 00:13:19,042
You're gonna say yes anyway,
so stop playing hard to get.

168
00:13:19,167 --> 00:13:20,708
Name your price.

169
00:13:21,083 --> 00:13:22,250
One million.

170
00:13:22,792 --> 00:13:24,958
Done.

171
00:13:25,083 --> 00:13:26,250
One million it is.

172
00:13:30,917 --> 00:13:32,375
Half upfront as a deposit.

173
00:13:33,958 --> 00:13:35,083
Wait a second.

174
00:13:36,875 --> 00:13:38,000
Look, Jeong-ha,

175
00:13:38,833 --> 00:13:42,250
you're not going to show your
face when you hit him, right?

176
00:13:43,833 --> 00:13:45,292
Let's be clear on this.

177
00:13:45,708 --> 00:13:48,125
If you get caught,

178
00:13:48,250 --> 00:13:49,917
leave me out of it.

179
00:13:52,417 --> 00:13:53,625
You hear me?

180
00:13:58,458 --> 00:13:59,708
What are you smirking at?

181
00:13:59,833 --> 00:14:02,553
Hiding behind someone else
because you're terrified of taking risks.

182
00:14:04,042 --> 00:14:05,333
It's pathetic.

183
00:14:07,750 --> 00:14:09,292
So we have a deal, right?

184
00:14:13,750 --> 00:14:15,292
I just wired you five hundred grand.

185
00:14:15,417 --> 00:14:16,417
Right?

186
00:14:16,708 --> 00:14:19,167
Don't make me waste my money.

187
00:14:32,292 --> 00:14:33,292
Were you waiting for me?

188
00:14:33,375 --> 00:14:34,125
Yeah.

189
00:14:34,250 --> 00:14:36,375
I didn't want to eat dinner alone.

190
00:14:47,708 --> 00:14:51,500
Your wrist... still hurts, doesn't it?

191
00:14:52,750 --> 00:14:53,958
Hey.

192
00:14:54,958 --> 00:14:57,000
Want to hear something I regret?

193
00:15:02,917 --> 00:15:05,917
I should've gotten hurt worse back then.

194
00:15:06,458 --> 00:15:08,143
Then I could've gotten a bigger payout
and put Grandma in a proper care facility.

195
00:15:08,167 --> 00:15:09,292
Hey.

196
00:15:10,083 --> 00:15:12,417
Other than that, I don't regret anything.

197
00:15:14,125 --> 00:15:15,542
It's not your fault.

198
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:19,625
Pass the Coke.

199
00:15:40,250 --> 00:15:41,708
What's this?

200
00:15:48,375 --> 00:15:49,133
Hey...

201
00:15:49,157 --> 00:15:51,458
It's what I borrowed from
you for Grandma's hospital bill.

202
00:15:52,375 --> 00:15:54,333
I'll pay back the rest next week.

203
00:15:54,458 --> 00:15:55,792
Where did you get this money?

204
00:15:56,125 --> 00:15:57,250
A part-time job.

205
00:15:57,375 --> 00:15:59,208
Say that one more time.

206
00:16:00,833 --> 00:16:04,000
Seriously, I started doing delivery runs.

207
00:16:05,250 --> 00:16:06,583
Stop doing that.

208
00:16:07,167 --> 00:16:09,167
Whatever it is, stop.

209
00:16:09,292 --> 00:16:10,852
I mean whatever you're doing right now.

210
00:16:14,292 --> 00:16:15,667
You finished eating?

211
00:16:23,708 --> 00:16:24,833
Borrowing this for a second.

212
00:16:24,958 --> 00:16:27,042
- Kim Jeong-ha.
- This is the last time.

213
00:16:29,875 --> 00:16:31,208
I won't do it again.

214
00:16:50,167 --> 00:16:55,125
(Incoming Call: Dad)

215
00:16:56,917 --> 00:16:58,750
School let out hours ago.

216
00:17:03,875 --> 00:17:05,292
What are you doing here?

217
00:17:07,917 --> 00:17:09,167
Running away.

218
00:17:16,625 --> 00:17:18,500
The counseling sheet...

219
00:17:18,625 --> 00:17:20,792
I was going to turn it in today.

220
00:17:21,917 --> 00:17:24,500
I tried to make up an
excuse, but I drew a blank.

221
00:17:25,833 --> 00:17:28,625
If you don't have one, just say
so. Did I tell you to make things up?

222
00:17:37,875 --> 00:17:39,375
The phone...

223
00:17:43,542 --> 00:17:45,417
I didn't steal it.

224
00:17:50,125 --> 00:17:51,458
I know.

225
00:17:58,042 --> 00:17:59,667
The chairman is asking for you, sir.

226
00:18:00,750 --> 00:18:02,000
See you tomorrow.

227
00:18:04,542 --> 00:18:06,667
It's late. Head straight home.

228
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:47,833
Is he in his room?

229
00:18:47,958 --> 00:18:49,000
Yes, sir.

230
00:19:02,083 --> 00:19:03,917
What? You stole a phone?

231
00:19:05,458 --> 00:19:06,875
Nothing to say for yourself?

232
00:19:08,167 --> 00:19:09,375
No, sir.

233
00:19:14,458 --> 00:19:17,058
Didn't I tell you to keep your
head down and stay out of trouble?

234
00:19:17,083 --> 00:19:18,250
Is that so hard?

235
00:19:18,375 --> 00:19:22,000
Pissing me off over
pocket change. Impressive.

236
00:19:23,458 --> 00:19:25,208
Are you going to keep playing dumb?

237
00:19:26,333 --> 00:19:27,542
Speak up!

238
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,958
Didn't two years in the
hospital teach you anything?

239
00:19:31,833 --> 00:19:33,167
Answer me, you little punk!

240
00:19:34,625 --> 00:19:35,792
Or what?

241
00:19:35,917 --> 00:19:39,458
Were you trying to sell it to scrape
together pocket money for your mother?

242
00:19:44,375 --> 00:19:47,175
Do you even remember what my mom looks like
to say something like that?

243
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:48,958
You ungrateful brat.

244
00:19:49,667 --> 00:19:51,667
If you truly feel sorry for her,

245
00:19:51,792 --> 00:19:54,833
stop humiliating me.

246
00:19:57,375 --> 00:19:59,417
What more do you want from me?

247
00:20:05,667 --> 00:20:07,125
Dong-jin!

248
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:09,725
Take him out and run him until he drops.

249
00:21:05,250 --> 00:21:07,792
What happened yesterday?
Why didn't you send photos?

250
00:21:08,042 --> 00:21:09,583
Get lost.

251
00:21:09,708 --> 00:21:11,125
You took care of it, right?

252
00:21:11,875 --> 00:21:13,875
Hey, didn't you take my deposit?

253
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,333
I told you to get lost.

254
00:21:15,833 --> 00:21:17,958
- Hey, Kim Jeong-ha!
- He told you to walk away.

255
00:21:20,542 --> 00:21:21,833
Morning homeroom is starting.

256
00:21:40,083 --> 00:21:41,708
We'll skip roll call today.

257
00:21:43,417 --> 00:21:44,500
Sir.

258
00:21:45,417 --> 00:21:47,000
Hyeon-jae isn't here yet.

259
00:21:47,667 --> 00:21:48,833
I know.

260
00:21:49,792 --> 00:21:51,708
Ji-woon, it's your turn
for counseling today.

261
00:21:51,833 --> 00:21:53,875
Come see me in the office after lunch.

262
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,667
Let me know when Hyeon-jae shows up.
That's all.

263
00:22:10,292 --> 00:22:11,333
Mr. Jang.

264
00:22:11,458 --> 00:22:13,208
Do you have a second to talk?

265
00:22:18,625 --> 00:22:20,125
Care for some coffee?

266
00:22:21,542 --> 00:22:22,708
Sure.

267
00:22:25,167 --> 00:22:27,208
I'll cut straight to the chase.

268
00:22:27,708 --> 00:22:29,500
About that phone incident.

269
00:22:29,625 --> 00:22:32,833
Let Hyeon-jae and
Young-moon settle it privately.

270
00:22:32,958 --> 00:22:34,500
Stay out of it.

271
00:22:35,083 --> 00:22:37,833
I don't think Hyeon-jae stole it.

272
00:22:38,583 --> 00:22:41,417
What if he already admitted it himself?

273
00:22:43,417 --> 00:22:45,375
Let him deal with it on his own.

274
00:22:46,375 --> 00:22:49,333
If he doesn't get along
with the others, let it be.

275
00:22:49,458 --> 00:22:52,458
If he can't fit in, don't force him to.

276
00:22:52,875 --> 00:22:56,625
Just let Hyeon-jae graduate quietly.

277
00:22:59,042 --> 00:23:00,708
Is that what the chairman wants?

278
00:23:03,417 --> 00:23:06,792
Just mark him down for sick leave today.

279
00:23:12,583 --> 00:23:13,917
Running away.

280
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:19,792
What's the reason?

281
00:23:20,708 --> 00:23:24,125
Sick leave doesn't
need an explanation, sir.

282
00:23:46,083 --> 00:23:47,417
You haven't left yet, sir.

283
00:23:53,667 --> 00:23:58,000
(Career Counseling Form)

284
00:24:03,167 --> 00:24:04,583
A day late.

285
00:24:05,458 --> 00:24:08,333
This was due yesterday.

286
00:24:11,625 --> 00:24:13,625
Didn't think you'd actually follow through.

287
00:24:17,667 --> 00:24:18,667
Goodbye, sir.

288
00:24:18,708 --> 00:24:19,917
Hyeon-jae.

289
00:24:23,292 --> 00:24:24,917
You're free right now, aren't you?

290
00:24:44,208 --> 00:24:45,500
You...

291
00:24:46,958 --> 00:24:48,792
You're always getting hurt.

292
00:24:51,917 --> 00:24:53,417
Does your father hit you?

293
00:25:01,083 --> 00:25:02,434
You should get psychological counseling.

294
00:25:02,458 --> 00:25:05,500
I'll arrange sessions
with the school counselor.

295
00:25:05,958 --> 00:25:08,500
Every Thursday.

296
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:10,875
Can you do that?

297
00:25:11,250 --> 00:25:12,458
No.

298
00:25:13,458 --> 00:25:15,500
I'm not asking for your permission.

299
00:25:17,750 --> 00:25:20,292
I don't want to talk
about myself to a stranger.

300
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:25,083
If I really have to do it...

301
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,250
Can I pick you?

302
00:26:02,125 --> 00:26:05,125
(Regret)
Do you want to meet up?

303
00:26:14,708 --> 00:26:15,833
I have.

304
00:26:15,958 --> 00:26:17,125
I've felt that way too.

305
00:26:17,958 --> 00:26:19,917
When I wanted to run away.

306
00:26:22,208 --> 00:26:24,458
I feel so completely worthless.

307
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:29,708
Even telling you all this
feels like running away.

308
00:26:39,917 --> 00:26:41,268
Let's leave the rest for tomorrow.

309
00:26:41,292 --> 00:26:42,875
- It's getting late.
- Sir.

310
00:26:45,375 --> 00:26:47,208
I want you to be the one who counsels me.

311
00:27:04,083 --> 00:27:05,583
Boy, with Caution.

312
00:27:06,042 --> 00:27:07,059
(Preview)
What are you doing?

313
00:27:07,083 --> 00:27:07,875
Are you out of your mind?

314
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:09,958
Say Jang Gi-woo's name again. I dare you.

315
00:27:10,083 --> 00:27:11,643
That is, if you really want
to find out how crazy I am.

316
00:27:11,667 --> 00:27:14,792
Did you only agree to
counseling because of me?

317
00:27:14,917 --> 00:27:15,917
Is that a problem?

318
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Didn't I tell you already?

319
00:27:18,125 --> 00:27:21,292
Stop getting involved with Hyeon-jae.

320
00:27:21,417 --> 00:27:24,458
I just want to know why.

321
00:27:24,917 --> 00:27:27,333
Didn't something happen
to you in the past, Mr. Jang?

322
00:27:27,583 --> 00:27:29,434
(Jang Gi-woo: Did you go to the hospital?)
Hit me.

323
00:27:29,458 --> 00:27:30,750
I told you to hit me.

324
00:27:31,167 --> 00:27:32,208
Hit me!

325
00:27:34,875 --> 00:27:36,792
Am I still getting special treatment?

326
00:27:37,333 --> 00:27:38,458
Am I?
